- @next: A victory for the incumbent AIADMK government of M G Ramachandran

@next

The victory can be attributed to the wave of sympathy across India for Indira Gandhi. Whose assasination earlier this year has triggered a surge in support for the INC and her son Rajiv Gandhi.

In addition, Chief Minister for Tamil Nadu M G Ramachandran had recently fallen ill generating even more sympathy for him and his party. The opposition DMK and its alliance lost seats and were also harmed by the INC's defection to the AIADMK alliance.

For us in Sri Lanka, it means a continuation of Tamil Nadu's support for the Tamil militants and their headbutting with the central government for further aid to them.